When you declare or alter a data view delegate within a BLC extension, the new
delegate is attached to the corresponding data view. To query a data view declared
within the base BLC or lower-level extension from the data view delegate, you should
redeclare the data view within the BLC extension. You do not need to redeclare a generic
PXSelect<Table> data member when it will not be used from the data view delegate.
For details, see Graph Extensions.
The redeclared data view delegate must have exactly the same signature—the return
value, the name of the method, and any method parameters— as the base data view
delegate.
