Implementing a Handler That is Appended to the Collection of Base
Handlers
When you define an event handler in the BLC extension class with the same declaration, as
it is defined in the base (original) BLC, this handler is added to the appropriate event handler
collection. Depending on the event type, the event handler is appended to either the end of
the collection or the start of it. When the event occurs, all event handlers in the collection
are executed, from the first one to the last one. For details, see Event Handlers.

